$ signet sandbox call --help
-- stdout --
Call a function of a deployed contract on a fork of the network, in the local
contract simulator. Nothing is submitted: the result says what the call would
return, write and require, at the fork's ledger.

Arguments are named: --arg handle=alice --arg wallet=G…. A value is read as
JSON when it parses as JSON and as a plain string otherwise, so --arg n=5 is
the number 5 and --arg handle=alice the string "alice"; quote a string that
looks like JSON (--arg name='"5"'). --args-file takes a JSON object instead.

Without --session every call starts from the fork. With --session <name>, the
call's writes are kept in the fork cache and the next call with the same name
starts from them; signet sandbox session reset <name> clears them.

The account a call runs as is --source-account (a G… address), not the root's
--source, which names the stellar identity signet signs with.

Time-dependent logic is tested by moving the ledger for the call:
--ledger-seq and --timestamp set it, --advance moves both from the fork's
(30d, 12h, or +N ledgers; one ledger is taken as the network's nominal 5s, an
approximation). An entry whose TTL runs out on the way reads as archived: the
call restores it, as the network does from protocol 23, and says which.
--unlimited lifts the budget to the sandbox's ceiling (10x the network's),
--budget-instructions sets the instruction limit. Every override shows in the
result's footer.

Usage:
  signet sandbox call <contract> <function> [flags]

Examples:
  signet sandbox call CASF…RCN count
  signet sandbox call CASF…RCN claim --arg handle=alice --arg wallet=GA5Z… --session demo
  signet sandbox call CASF…RCN resolve --arg handle=alice --session demo
  signet sandbox call CASF…RCN count --wasm ./target/wasm32v1-none/release/registry.wasm
  signet sandbox call CASF…RCN claim --arg unlock_time=1790000000 --advance 30d

Flags:
      --advance string             move the ledger forward from the fork's: a duration (30d, 12h, 90m) or +N ledgers, at a nominal 5s per ledger
      --arg stringArray            a named argument, name=value (JSON, or a plain string); repeat for each
      --args-file string           a JSON file holding an object of named arguments
      --auth string                how require_auth is answered: record (approve and list it; signatures unchecked), strict (also refuse auth below the root call), enforce (check --auth-entries) (default "record")
      --auth-entries string        with --auth enforce: a JSON array of pre-signed base64 SorobanAuthorizationEntry
      --budget-instructions uint   run under this CPU instruction limit (up to 10x the network's)
  -h, --help                       help for call
      --ledger-seq uint32          run the call at this ledger sequence
      --session string             keep this call's writes under a name, and start from that name's earlier writes
      --source-account string      the account (G…) the call runs as
      --timestamp string           run the call at this ledger close time (Unix seconds or RFC 3339)
      --unlimited                  run under the sandbox's budget ceiling (10x the network's limits)
      --wasm string                swap this local WASM in first, as an upgrade would, keeping storage

Global Flags:
      --context string              deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --drift string                when an entry fetched for the fork changed on-chain after the fork ledger: warn, fail (exit 6), or refork (pin the latest ledger and run once more) (default "warn")
      --insecure                    allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                        write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string              Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --network-passphrase string   passphrase of a custom --network (checked against the RPC's getNetwork)
      --rpc-url string              Stellar RPC to fork from (overrides the context's rpc-url; testnet defaults to https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org)
      --sign-with-key string        identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string               identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string                  Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)
-- stderr --
(empty)
-- exit 0 --
